{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ModelsOfQous.MainCommutativeDiagram","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ModelsOfQous.MainCommutativeDiagram","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.diagram_commutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.diagram_commutes","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L73-L89","doc":"**The diagram commutes.**\n\nBoth paths from the jet bundle to the Schrödinger corner agree:\ngoing right along the Euler–Lagrange arrow and then down the\n`q → 1` edge gives `(1 − q⁻¹) · einsteinValue`, while going down\nthe q-linearisation arrow and then right along parallel transport\ngives `schrodingerValue`.\n\nCommutativity is **derived** from the three arrow equations, not\nassumed: it was formerly a fourth field `commutativity` of\n`MainCommutativeDiagram`, which made this statement a restatement\nof its own hypothesis. The chain is\n`(1 − q⁻¹)·einstein = (1 − q⁻¹)·jet = section = schrodinger`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:main-commutative-diagram","label":"prop:main-commutative-diagram","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.q_linearisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.q_linearisation","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Left arrow: q-linearisation of jet data gives sections. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.parallel_transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.parallel_transport","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Bottom arrow: parallel transport maps sections to Schrödinger. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.euler_lagrange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.euler_lagrange","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Top arrow: Euler–Lagrange operator maps jets to field equations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.schrodingerValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.schrodingerValue","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Bottom-right corner: Schrödinger evolution value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.sectionValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.sectionValue","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L63-L63","doc":"Bottom-left corner: linearized section value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.einsteinValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.einsteinValue","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Top-right corner: Einstein tensor value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.jetValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.jetValue","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Top-left corner: jet data (connection strength). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.q_qInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.q_qInv","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Defining relation `q · q⁻¹ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.qInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.qInv","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The inverse indeterminate `q⁻¹`. Over `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` the\nindeterminate is invertible; `qInv` names that inverse explicitly,\nsince `R_q` is a `CommRing` without a global `Inv` instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.q","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The substrate parameter q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MainCommutativeDiagram","kind":"structure","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L38-L71","doc":"**Main commutative diagram data**.\n\nThe four corners of the diagram are:\n1. Jet bundle J¹(S) (geometric, nonlinear)\n2. Einstein field equations (gravity)\n3. Linearized sections Γ(S) (quantum, linear)\n4. Schrödinger equation (quantum mechanics)\n\nThe substrate parameter q mediates between geometric (gravity)\nand quantum (Schrödinger) descriptions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/main-commutative-diagram.lean#L32-L34","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}